<Routines>
<Routine Name="a1_MainRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[
All information provided  - No Warranty or implied merchantability. 
Refer to the RSLogix 5000 End User License Agreement (EULA) in the Release Notes.

]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[NOP();]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==================================================================
Sample program for Kinematics feature, via  MCT programming ;
with Source coordinate_system=CS_XYZ (3 Virtual axes, Geometry=Cartesian)
and  Target  coordinate_system=Delta3D (3 Joint axes, Geometry=Delta 3D)   
====   ==== ==== ==== ==== ==== ====
Using  Multi-Axis Linear moves MCLM in AOI Logix to exercise a PICK & PLACE cycle. 
in PickPlace AIO: pass in Velocity, & the AIO calculates the Acc/Dec for Speed-invariant Path 
open Trend=  to view the Position plot of the resulting Pick & Place profile.   
==================================================================]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[JSR(VectorDynamics,0) ,JSR(TimerRoutine,0) ,JSR(a3_PICK_PLACE,0) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[==========================
USER SETUP:::
Toggle bits from left to right.
===========================
 a2_MCTTurnOn: Enables the Transformation between the Cartesian axes and Robot axes
InitialPos: Moves to the inital Cartesian Position(HorizDistance/2, 0, -620)
PICKPLACE: Does a PICK and PLACE with a speed invariant path..See Z_help for more details
]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(a2_mctTurnOn)XIC(InitialPos)XIC(PickPlace)OTU(unlatch);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Status & Monitor the [Source's cartesian] Axis Position]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[[XIC(CS_XYZ.TransformSourceStatus) ,XIC(Delta3D.TransformTargetStatus) ]MOV(CS_XYZ.ActualPosition[0],Actual_Position_axis[0])MOV(CS_XYZ.ActualPosition[1],Actual_Position_axis[1])MOV(CS_XYZ.ActualPosition[2],Actual_Position_axis[2]);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[MOV(T_CycleFrequency,Pick_cycles_per_minute);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="a3_PICK_PLACE" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(s:fs)MOV(-1,step);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(HorizDistBack,-HorizontalDistance)CPT(CommandTolerance,CommandTolerance)CPT(posArray[0],-HorizontalDistance/2);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[SSV(COORDINATESYSTEM,CS_XYZ,CommandPositionTolerance,CommandTolerance);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(MotionGroup.GroupSynced)XIC(a2_mctTurnOn)MCT(CS_XYZ,Delta3D,mct1,ort[0],trs[0])OTU(a2_mctTurnOn);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="4" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(InitialPos)MCLM(CS_XYZ,InitialMclm1,0,posArray[0],CartSpeed,Units per sec,PickPlace1.AccDecDisplay,Units per sec2,PickPlace1.AccDecDisplay,Units per sec2,S-Curve,100.0,100.0,% of Time,TermType1,0,Programmed,0,0,None,0,0)OTU(InitialPos);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="5" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Add-On Instruction for PICK PLACE -  Specify the velocity to  the AOI and it calculates
 the required ACC/ DEC for speed-invariant path.]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(PickPlace)EQU(step,-1)[PICKPLACE(PickPlace1,CS_XYZ,HorizontalDistance,UpDistance,Downdistance,CartSpeed) ,XIC(PickPlace1.PC) MOV(1,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="6" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,1)[PICKPLACE(PickPlace2,CS_XYZ,HorizDistBack,Downdistance,UpDistance,CartSpeed) ,XIC(PickPlace2.PC) MOV(-1,step) ];]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="TimerRoutine" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[This routine claculates the number of PICK-PLACE 's per minute.
T_Cyclefrequency displays the value]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[EQU(step,1)CTU(Counter,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[RTO(CycleTime,?,?);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="2" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[XIC(Counter.DN)CPT(TimeinSeconds,CycleTime.ACC/((Counter.PRE-1)*1000))RES(Counter)RES(CycleTime);]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="3" Type="N">
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(T_CycleFrequency,60.0/(TimeinSeconds+.00001));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="VectorDynamics" Type="RLL">
<RLLContent>
<Rung Number="0" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Vector velocity of Cartesian Coordinate System]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VectorVelocity,SQR(X.ActualVelocity**2 + Y.ActualVelocity**2+Z.ActualVelocity**2));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
<Rung Number="1" Type="N">
<Comment>
<![CDATA[Vector Acceleration of the cartesian Cooridnate system]]>
</Comment>
<Text>
<![CDATA[CPT(VectorAcceleration,SQR(X.CommandAcceleration**2+Y.CommandAcceleration**2+Z.CommandAcceleration**2));]]>
</Text>
</Rung>
</RLLContent>
</Routine>
<Routine Name="Z_help" Type="ST">
<STContent>
<Line Number="0">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="1">
<![CDATA[(*]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="2">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="3">
<![CDATA[                  DELTA Geometry PICK - PLACE CYCLE AOI Overview ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="4">
<![CDATA[ /*  ============================================================================= */	]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="5">
<![CDATA[         ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="6">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="7">
<![CDATA[ Open a1_mainRoutine and  toggle the bits from left to right. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="8">
<![CDATA[    ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="9">
<![CDATA[                     __________________________  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="10">
<![CDATA[                  A |    HorizontalDistance    | C]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="11">
<![CDATA[       Updistance   |                          |  DownDistance]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="12">
<![CDATA[                    |                          |]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="13">
<![CDATA[                  B |                          | D    ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="14">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="15">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="16">
<![CDATA[  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="17">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="18">
<![CDATA[UpDistance         =  Pick distance       ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="19">
<![CDATA[Downdistance       =  Place distance ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="20">
<![CDATA[HorizontalDistance =  The width of the PICK-PLACE Cycle (Pick and Place distance vaues can be set with different values)  ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="21">
<![CDATA[CartSpeed          =  PICK-PLACE cycle speed]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="22">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="23">
<![CDATA[CommandTolerance   = Set the command tolerance equal to half the horizontal distance for maximum blending.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="24">
<![CDATA[					 If clearance is required during PICK nad PLACE, set it equal to Updistance minus Clearance distance required.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="25">
<![CDATA[             ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="26">
<![CDATA[For example: AB = UpDistance = 80 mm and you require 10 mm clearance from B, then set ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="27">
<![CDATA[CommandTolerance =  70 mm.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="28">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="29">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="30">
<![CDATA[The  Acc/Dec for the PICK-PLACE values are computed in the AOI based on the CartSpeed value that the user specifies. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="31">
<![CDATA[ ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="32">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="33">
<![CDATA[T_cyclefrequency tag displays the number of pick and place cycles.]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="34">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="35">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="36">
<![CDATA[Note: All moves are incremental. ]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="37">
<![CDATA[]]>
</Line>
<Line Number="38">
<![CDATA[*)]]>
</Line>
</STContent>
</Routine>
</Routines>
</Program>
